  {
   "type": "text",
   "html": "<h2>How to procedurally generate DMF file for inflatable structures?</h2>"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "html": "<p>June 2023 - August 2023 at <a href=\"https://www.pneu.haus/\">Pneuhaus</a> under guidance of August Lekrecke.</p>\n<p>Over the 8 weeks, I developed C# scripts in Grasshopper for generating production files for inflatable structures. This workflow accelerates entire design process, from form-finding, patterning, labeling, unrolling, and simulation, adaptable to various input topologies and pattern types. It uses the half-edge data structure to enhance performance and robustness.</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "image",
   "src": "inflatable-patterner/02.jpg",
   "width": 2400,
   "height": 1350,
   "caption": "Inflatable Structure example 1: Cloud Lights by Pneuhaus"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "html": "<h2><strong>Solution 1: Closed Boundaries (2D Input)</strong></h2>\n<p>Turn almost any flat doodle drawing into manufacturable inflatable.</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "row",
   "columns": [
    {
     "flex": 0.5,
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "image",
       "src": "inflatable-patterner/03.jpg",
       "width": 2400,
       "height": 2040,
       "caption": "Some input tests"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "flex": 0.5,
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "loop",
       "src": "/media/inflatable-patterner/04.mp4",
       "width": 2600,
       "height": 2210,
       "caption": "Developable Panels"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "html": "<h3>The grasshopper definition enables users to freely modify the patterning design for aesthetic, structural, and manufacturing purposes. The segmentation count, length, width, seam alignment, and other parameters can all be easily adjusted based on the needs.</h3>"
  },
